---
// Home (site-prelaunch.md §2) — copy verbatim from ai-team/pm/site-copy-twiceover.md
// "Page: Home". Do not reword (PM #41); flag issues to PM.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="TwiceOver — a second look at your own book"
  description="TwiceOver connects to your brokerage read-only and lays out the math, the levels, and the context on the positions you already hold — measured against your own rules."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1 class="type-display">A second look at your own book.</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      TwiceOver connects to your brokerage <strong>read-only</strong> and lays out the math, the
      levels, and the context on the positions you already hold — measured against
      <strong>your own rules</strong>. You read it. You decide.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn-quiet" href="/pricing">See pricing</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="what-you-see">
    <h2 id="what-you-see" class="type-heading-1 section-heading">What you see <span class="aside">(the first two come from your connected account; the rest, on any ticker)</span></h2>
    <ul class="what-grid">
      <li class="card">
        <h3 class="type-heading-2">Your structure, with the math <span class="tag">(connected)</span></h3>
        <p>your legs grouped into the position you actually hold, with net debit/credit, breakevens, max profit, max loss, and current P&amp;L.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="card">
        <h3 class="type-heading-2">Your rules, on live data <span class="tag">(connected)</span></h3>
        <p>the profit targets, DTE thresholds, and max-loss lines <em>you</em> configured, evaluated against where the position is right now.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="card">
        <h3 class="type-heading-2">Levels &amp; context</h3>
        <p>key technical levels, options-structure context, the macro/regime backdrop, and curated signal — each with its source and timestamp.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="card">
        <h3 class="type-heading-2">A menu of paths, with the full math</h3>
        <p>the structures in front of you, each with its complete numbers and trigger levels. No ranking, no "do this." The conclusion is yours.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="how-it-works">
    <h2 id="how-it-works" class="type-heading-1 section-heading">How it works</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <p><span class="step-title">Analyze any ticker — connect read-only when you're ready.</span> Without connecting, you get the full analysis on any ticker as a new idea. Connect your brokerage <strong>read-only</strong> to read your <em>actual</em> positions and balances against <strong>your own rules</strong> — TwiceOver can never place, change, or cancel orders, and never touches your funds.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <p><span class="step-title">It does the synthesis.</span> Live licensed market and options data, key levels, macro context — and, when you're connected, your actual positions and your own rules — combined into one read.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
        <p><span class="step-title">You decide.</span> Every read is indicative: it describes the state and the math of each path. You make the call.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="what-its-not">
    <h2 id="what-its-not" class="type-heading-1 section-heading">What TwiceOver is <em>not</em></h2>
    <div class="not-block">
      <p>Not an investment adviser. No recommendations, no trading signals, no "buy" or "sell." It never executes trades and never holds your money. It is a data-analytics tool that helps you understand your own positions — you bring the judgment.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="pricing-cue"><a href="/pricing">See plans</a> · <span class="muted">Launching soon.</span></p>
</Base>
